Cudy TR3600 v1: make the fan curve actually cool (kill the dead 25 % step)

0006 moved the trips to 65/75/85 C but also changed cooling-levels to
<0 64 160 255>, which makes level 1 a 25 % PWM step (64/255).  Measured on
the board with each level forced for 80 s (6 samples, fan in manual mode):

  level 0 (off)     64.1 C
  level 1 (25 %)    63.7 C   <- cannot cool at all
  level 2 (63 %)    61.3 C
  level 3 (100 %)   58.0 C

A step that does not cool is worse than no step: the step_wise governor
walks up to level 1 at 65 C, sees no temperature drop, and the SoC keeps
climbing until the 75 C step.  Restore the upstream 50 % step and space the
rest out:

  cooling-levels = <0 128 200 255>   (off / 50 % / 78 % / 100 %)

Second problem: this board idles at ~64 C with the fan stopped, which is
almost exactly the 65 C trip 0006 introduced, so the fan sits right on the
threshold and starts on any small load.  Move the whole ramp up so the
board stays silent at idle and only spins up under real load:

  < 63 C : off            (idle sits at ~64 C, fan stopped)
  68 C   : level 1, PWM 128 (50 %)
  78 C   : level 2, PWM 200 (78 %)
  88 C   : level 3, PWM 255 (100 %)

The hysteresis stays at 5 C, so the fan releases at 63 C.  The SoC has a
125 C critical trip and the CPU-throttling trip is at 117 C, so the 88 C
top step still leaves a 29 C margin - the unit is nowhere near thermal
trouble, this is purely about noise at idle versus cooling under load.

cooling-levels keeps four entries because the tr3600-fan daemon and its
LuCI page only accept levels 0-3.

Verified by compiling the patched DTS: the trips resolve to 68/78/88 C with
5 C hysteresis, no duplicate trips are created, and cooling-levels has
exactly four entries.

Signed-off-by: TR3600 build kit <noreply@example.com>
---
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987b-cudy-tr3600-v1.dts
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987b-cudy-tr3600-v1.dts
@@ -83,7 +83,7 @@
 &fan {
 	fan-supply = <&fan_3p3v>;
 	pwms = <&pwm 0 50000 0>;
-	cooling-levels = <0 64 160 255>;
+	cooling-levels = <0 128 200 255>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
@@ -284,10 +284,14 @@
 
 /*
  * mt7987.dtsi maps the 40 C trip to fan level 1, which leaves the fan
- * spinning at 50 % from 40 C upwards - clearly audible at idle (the unit
- * sits around 57 C doing nothing).  Move the first step up to 65 C and use
- * a gentler ramp.  The vendor DTS keeps the fan off below 85 C; 65 C keeps
- * a usable margin without the constant noise.
+ * spinning at 50 % from 40 C upwards - clearly audible at idle.  This board
+ * idles at ~64 C with the fan stopped, so the whole ramp is moved up: the
+ * fan stays off at idle and only spins up under real load.
+ *
+ *   < 63 C : off            (idle sits at ~64 C, fan stopped)
+ *   68 C   : level 1, PWM 128 (50 %)
+ *   78 C   : level 2, PWM 200 (78 %)
+ *   88 C   : level 3, PWM 255 (100 %)
  *
  * cooling-levels stays at four states (0..3) because the tr3600-fan daemon
  * and its LuCI page only accept levels 0-3.
@@ -295,17 +299,17 @@
 &cpu_thermal {
 	trips {
 		cpu_trip_active_low: active-low {
-			temperature = <65000>;
+			temperature = <68000>;
 			hysteresis = <5000>;
 		};
 
 		cpu_trip_active_med: active-med {
-			temperature = <75000>;
+			temperature = <78000>;
 			hysteresis = <5000>;
 		};
 
 		cpu_trip_active_high: active-high {
-			temperature = <85000>;
+			temperature = <88000>;
 			hysteresis = <5000>;
 		};
 	};
